course: dictionary
lesson: 9054
title: Sleepwalking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sleepwalking means getting up and walking around while you are still asleep. You may move about, open doors or go downstairs, but your eyes stay shut and you are not awake. «Sleepwalking happens in deep sleep, not while dreaming.»
explain: The word can also mean doing something without thinking or noticing, as if you were asleep. If someone is so busy they go through the day sleepwalking, they are not really paying attention to what they are doing.
explain: Sleepwalking is common in children and is usually harmless. Most children grow out of it. «A sleepwalker should be guided gently back to bed, not shouted at.» Families often lock doors or put gates on stairs to keep a sleepwalker safe.
fact: Sleepwalking means walking around while you are still asleep.
fact: Sleepwalking usually happens in deep sleep, not while you are dreaming.
fact: «Waking a sleepwalker is not dangerous, just confusing.»
fact: Sleepwalking can also mean doing something without thinking, as if asleep.
fact: Sleepwalking is a noun, and the verb is sleepwalk: he sleepwalks, he sleepwalked, he is sleepwalking.
exercise: «Sleepwalking happens in deep sleep, not while dreaming.» What is sleepwalking? | *Getting up and walking around while still asleep | Walking to school in the rain | Waking up very early | Having a very long dream
exercise: «A sleepwalker should be guided gently back to bed, not shouted at.» What should you do? | *Guide them gently back to bed | Leave them on the stairs and go to sleep | Shout until they wake up properly | Wake them with a loud bang
exercise: Dad says Sam was sleepwalking through his homework, not noticing a thing. What does he mean? | *Doing it without thinking, as if asleep | Doing it outside in the garden | Doing it with his eyes wide open | Doing it very quickly and neatly
test: «Children usually grow out of sleepwalking.» What does grow out of mean here? | *Stop doing it as they get older | Fall out of bed | Grow taller than before | Make it bigger each night
test: Is waking a sleepwalker dangerous? | *No, it is not dangerous, just confusing | Yes, they will never sleep again | Only if they are dreaming | Yes, it can hurt them badly
exam: Which statement is true? | *Sleepwalking is common in children and is usually harmless | Sleepwalking always lasts for your whole life | Sleepwalking happens only when you are dreaming | Sleepwalkers should be shouted at to wake them
